{
 "_about": "EVERY ACTION, ONE ROW EACH (owner, 17 Nov). `name` is what a phone posts (or `?run=` names, with `run: true`); `handler` the backend function it reaches; `roles` the permission tiers that may (anyone = signed out, member = signed in, child, admin; a tier's roles are settings.json `roles`), by name where it can: `tiers` for every tier, or a settings.json `roles.may` word (signedIn, grownUp), never a tier list written out (tools/one-list.js); `feature` listed in the payload's `features` so a phone can tell what this deploy can do; `arg` a job that takes `&arg=`. A handler still checks WHOSE row it is — the gate only checks who is signed in. `node tools/permissions.js` writes ACTION_ACCESS and RUNNABLE (access.gs), postActions_ (dopost.gs), payloadFeatures_ (get-start.gs), PERMISSIONS (booking.gs) and permissions.json from this; edit here, never there.",
 "_items": "`items`: what the `item` door (door get/save/delete) answers, by kind:verb — the tiers allowed (permissions.json item rows, itemMay_), the handler for your own (`handler`) and for an admin asking after somebody else (`other`; `logged` leaves a lens_log row, `blank` lets an admin ask for none), `library` read by the library reader (no handler: a library write is the tools` libImport), every kind:verb with a handler is listed in the payload`s `features`. No tiers: refused for everybody. STEP 6 (22 Nov): a plain read, save, delete or list of one kind is an item here; its old action name is a row with `item` (kind:verb) and no tiers or handler of its own, taking the item`s handler and its tiers from the table; The handler is handed kind:verb, by the item door and by the old name alike, and never the old name. The door answers `list` as it does `get`. tools/one-action-roles.js fails the build if any old name is now open wider.",
